# Rank 1631 / CVE-2017-6503: qBittorrent displayed torrent metadata and
# peer-supplied strings in Qt rich-text widgets and in the shared logger
# without HTML escaping, so a crafted torrent's comment, creator string or
# peer client name executed as markup in the GUI (cross-site scripting
# through a desktop rich-text label, CWE-79; GHSA-rhmh-8w93-hhpf cites
# commit 6ca3e4f0 directly). loadTorrentInfos in
# src/gui/properties/propertieswidget.cpp did
#
#   comment_text->setText(Utils::Misc::parseHtmlLinks(m_torrent->comment()));
#   label_created_by_val->setText(m_torrent->creator());
#
# where comment_text and label_created_by_val are QLabel widgets declared in
# the .ui file, and QLabel renders rich text by default (Qt::AutoText). The
# same unescaped values reach PeerListWidget::addPeer/updatePeer
# (peer.client()), DeletionConfirmationDlg (the torrent name) and
# Logger::addMessage/addPeer, whose stored rows the Web UI also displays.
# The fixed revision adds Utils::String::toHtmlEscaped (Qt's toHtmlEscaped/Qt::escape
# under one name) and wraps all five sites. The vulnerable construct is
# present at the parent and the remediation at the commit; no pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, no receiver-type fact for a C++ instance call. QLabel::setText
# is the natural code.HtmlRender sink and Qt documents it as rich text, but
# the C++ frontend lowers the call to callee.path "comment_text.setText"
# where the receiver segment is the variable name: `QLabel *a` and
# `QLineEdit *b` produce identical token forms (verified with vyql graph --
# both lower to <var>.setText, no type anywhere), and no tree-sitter
# frontend emits recv_type (Java only). A bare `setText` binding therefore
# cannot be told from QLineEdit::setText, QPushButton::setText or
# QStandardItem::setData, and this tree alone holds 323 setText/setData
# sites over 97 receiver variables, overwhelmingly plain-text controls --
# the same loadTorrentInfos also calls setText with a hex info-hash and a
# locale-formatted date. That is the bare-common-name shape, not a sink.
# The source dies the same way: the untrusted values arrive through the
# application's own getters (TorrentHandle::comment/creator, thin wrappers
# over libtorrent's torrent_info accessors), whose in-tree paths end at
# `m_nativeInfo->comment()` -- again keyed on a receiver variable, and
# comment/creator are ordinary getter names across every C++ tree. Worse,
# the widget members are declared in Qt-Designer-generated ui_*.h headers
# that are build artifacts absent from the repository, so the receiver type
# is not in the tree at all for the real sites. Measured on the real code:
# 440 findings at the parent, none on any of the four files' display calls
# (the logger.cpp and peerlistwidget.cpp rows are IntegerSizeArithmeticSink
# on counter arithmetic), and identical at the fixed revision. The ENGINE-GAPS entry
# for this rank records the missing receiver-type fact. No definition
# change shipped. Both cases reject VYQL-INJ-004; when a receiver-type fact
# and a Qt rich-text sink land, the unescaped form must flip to expect.
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1631: torrent metadata shown in a rich-text label unescaped"
  lang cpp
  file src/gui/properties/propertieswidget.cpp
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  void PropertiesWidget::loadTorrentInfos(BitTorrent::TorrentHandle *const torrent)
  {
      clear();
      m_torrent = torrent;
      if (!m_torrent) return;

      hash_lbl->setText(m_torrent->hash());
      if (m_torrent->hasMetadata()) {
          // Comment
          comment_text->setText(Utils::Misc::parseHtmlLinks(m_torrent->comment()));

          label_created_by_val->setText(m_torrent->creator());
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1631: the fixed revision escapes metadata before the label"
  lang cpp
  file src/gui/properties/propertieswidget.cpp
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  void PropertiesWidget::loadTorrentInfos(BitTorrent::TorrentHandle *const torrent)
  {
      clear();
      m_torrent = torrent;
      if (!m_torrent) return;

      hash_lbl->setText(m_torrent->hash());
      if (m_torrent->hasMetadata()) {
          // Comment
          comment_text->setText(Utils::Misc::parseHtmlLinks(
              Utils::String::toHtmlEscaped(m_torrent->comment())));

          label_created_by_val->setText(Utils::String::toHtmlEscaped(m_torrent->creator()));
      }
  }
  ```
